Error [E0112]: `sqrt` needs Float or F32, not Int (a whole number)
  --> tests/ui/core_math_float_type_mismatch.jet:4:15
    |
  4 |     math.sqrt(1)
    |               ^
 Why: math functions in this family operate on floating-point numbers
 Fix: pass a Float or F32 value

Error [E0112]: `is_nan` needs Float or F32, not Int (a whole number)
  --> tests/ui/core_math_float_type_mismatch.jet:5:17
    |
  5 |     math.is_nan(1)
    |                 ^
 Why: floating-point classification only applies to floats
 Fix: pass a Float or F32 value

Error [E0112]: `sign` needs Float or F32, not Int (a whole number)
  --> tests/ui/core_math_float_type_mismatch.jet:6:15
    |
  6 |     math.sign(1)
    |               ^
 Why: sign classifies a floating-point value as negative, zero, or positive
 Fix: pass a Float or F32 value

Error [E0112]: `pow` needs both arguments to have the same float type, but base is Float (a decimal number) and exponent is F32 (a 32-bit decimal number)
  --> tests/ui/core_math_float_type_mismatch.jet:7:23
    |
  7 |     math.pow(2.0, F32.from_float(2.0) ?? F32.from_int(0))
    |                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: D-FLOATW1: mixing float widths is not allowed — use the same width for both
 Fix: convert with `F32.from_float(value)` or `Float.from_f32(value)` to match

Error [E0112]: `hypot` needs all arguments to have the same float type
  --> tests/ui/core_math_float_type_mismatch.jet:8:25
    |
  8 |     math.hypot(2.0, F32.from_float(2.0) ?? F32.from_int(0))
    |                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: D-FLOATW1: mixing float widths is not allowed
 Fix: convert the arguments to the same float width
